# Dedicated audit-chain MAC key: exactly 32 bytes encoded as 64 lowercase hex
# characters (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Copy to "audit_mac_secret", chmod 600,
# and preserve it across root-token rotation. First deployments also create an
# empty sibling file `audit_mac_previous_secrets` and use key version 1. On a
# deliberate audit-key rotation, that sibling receives `old-version:64hex`
# entries while the non-secret MINDPATTERN_AUDIT_MAC_KEY_VERSION increments.
# See docs/INCIDENT_RUNBOOK.md; never paste actual key bytes into this example.
